@startuml
title EventBook Component and Deployment Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Customer /\nAdministrator" as User
package "Browser environment" {
  component "Web client\nindex.html · style.css · app.js" as Web
  database "Browser local storage\nsession + favourites" as Local
}
node "Ubuntu EC2 / local Node environment" {
  component "Nginx reverse proxy\nTCP 80" as Nginx
  component "PM2\neventbook process manager" as PM2
  component "Node.js HTTP server\nlocalhost:3000" as Node
  component "Application services\nauth/session · role checks\nevent validation · booking/cancellation\ncapacity protection · health endpoint" as Services
  database "data.json\nEvent [0..*] · Booking [0..*]" as Data
}

User --> Web : UI actions
Web <--> Local : session + favourites
Web --> Nginx : HTTP static assets + JSON API
Nginx --> Node : proxy request
PM2 --> Node : supervises/restarts
Node --> Services : routes request
Services <--> Data : read/write records

note bottom of Web
Demo card fields remain in the browser and are never sent to the API.
end note
note bottom of Services
Authorise role and validate whole quantity/capacity before persistence.
end note
note bottom of Nginx
EC2 local PM2/Nginx/API checks passed. Public network requests timed out upstream.
end note
@enduml
